s  An obvious tumor is not identified  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominantly fatty with a moderate amount of pink white fibrous stroma  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral end margins in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the medial end margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the lateral end margin     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the breast parenchyma with inked margins   biopsy cavity  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast final margin   are 5 irregularly outlined   unoriented fragments of fibrofatty breast tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  All of the fragments are serially sectioned  The breast parenchyma consists predominantly of fatty tissue  The larger 3 fragments are entirely but separately submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The smaller 2 fragments are entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 06   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 39 47AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Re Excision PART B  Breast  Right  Final Margin   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
