cimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely from A through F  Labeled  Left axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are present with the largest one being 1 5cm in greatest dimension  which are entirely submitted in G through I  Labeled  Left breast additional medial tissue  is a piece of amorphous  unoriented fibrous tissue  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  It is inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white gray areas admixed with yellow adipose tissue without conspicious borders  Entirely submitted in J through L  Labeled  Additional left axillary nodes  are two small firm lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  which are submitted in cassette M  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Gerri Wittrock  ANP PART A  LEFT BREAST  SPECIMEN  1   LUMPECTOMY  PART B  LEFT BREAST  SPECIMEN  2   ADDITIONAL MEDIAL TISSU PART C  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART D  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   ADDITIONAL    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm pink and yellow tissue which is submitted in toto to cassette A  Gross Description by  DANIEL ALMGREN Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Jaime L Kline  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY , Unchecked.
