Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 11 CLINICAL DATA  33 year old lady with left breast infiltrating ductal carcinoma with intraductal component  Re excision      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  CORRECTED INTRA OPERATIVE PATHOLOGIST Revised by  Teri L  Moore  MD Revised on 23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 07 15                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   REEXCISION  FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  AND FOREIGN BODY REACTION CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL MALIGNANCY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  There is marked chronic inflammation with fat necrosis and histiocytic reaction in the permanent slide made from the frozen section tissue  however  carcinoma is not seen  It is not possible to locate the frozen section slide to confirm the frozen section diagnosis of malignancy  and it is possible the fat necrosis with inflammation represents the area interpreted as malignant on frozen section  AXILLA  LEFT  NODES   EXCISION  2 of 19 LYMPH NODES POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  MICROMETASTASES   Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 31                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lumpectomy specimen with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm with a central healed scar along its length  Two sutures designating the medial resection margin and one suture designating the superior resection margin are present  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm cavity that is lined by tan brown  shaggy surface  The cavity is 0 6cm from the medi