inomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  The first specimen consists of an unoriented  20 x 17 x 4cm radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying 19 x 10cm ellipse of skin with unremarkable nipple  There is an 11 x 8 x 2cm portion of tissue projected from the main specimen  presumablY the axillary tail  There is a 5cm  well healed  curvilinear biopsy site present 3 5cm superior to the nipple  Beneath this scar is a palpable  firm mass  The area over the mass is inked black  Cross sectioning reveals a large  4 x 7 x 3 5cm biopsy cavity filled with serosanguineous fluid  The tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity is very soft  yellow  and friable  The tissue surrounding the biopsy site on the superficial side is very firm  and appears to abut the overlying skin  This margin is in A  The biopsy cavity comes to within 1 2cm of the deep surface  The deep surface margin is in B  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity are in C E  The tissue away from the breast cavity appears unremarkable  Representative sections are in F and G  The axillary tail is dissected  revealing multiple lymph nodes which are bisected and half submitted in G K  One of the nodes is suspicious for metastatic carcinoma  with a very firm  homogeneous  white tan surface  This node is in I  Designated  right axillary nodes  are two tissue fragments measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Several lymph nodes are identified  bisected  and half submitted in J M  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                               