Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA  Excision of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FLORID SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH FOCAL MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND FOCAL BLUNT DUCT ADENOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE SOLID PAPILLARY CARCINOMA WITH FOCAL MUCIN PRODUCTION  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  FLORID SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH FOCAL MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 20 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  Specimen  2  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast needle biopsy  is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue containing a guide wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a yellow red fatty parenchyma  Entirely submitted in cassettes A through H  Labeled  left breast lumpectomy  is a 6 x 4 x 1 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue containing a guide wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm slightly firm  hemorrhagic area that is 0 9cm from the closest inked margin  Representative sections with hemorrhagic area is frozen as FX  1  now resubmitted as I  The remainder of the tissue around the lesion is submitted in cassettes J through L  Representative sections away from the lesion are submitted in cassettes M through Q  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  TWO FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASION  AWAIT PERMANENT  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  1  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Yes.
