e tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained     The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained     HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is  evaluated visually and reported as follows     Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or  incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells     Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells     Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision            Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 19 26      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH Quantitation Analyisis    FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION    BREAST  LEFT  CELLBLOCK  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified    See note     Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  477  to  chromosome 17 signals  49  in 30 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE  or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17  polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis     The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be  interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification    Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID             Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 17 46       CLINICAL HISTORY  46 year old female status